From e55e01096b0e3408139e194b705c13e9566d1ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:39:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hp39gii: the defconfig turned its own paging option off

CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGING=y was followed by the stale
"# CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGING is not set" left over from when paging shipped
disabled.  The last occurrence wins, so a fresh configure.sh followed by
make olddefconfig resolved paging to "n" -- and STMP3770_KHICAS depends on
it, so a kernel built from this defconfig had no KhiCAS and no .pgtext
section at all.  Local builds never noticed because they reuse an older
.config and never re-resolve it.

Verified in a clean checkout: configure.sh hp39gii:nsh + make olddefconfig
now yields CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGING=y and CONFIG_STMP3770_KHICAS=y.
---
 boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig b/boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig
index f116ecc6..498a778a 100644
--- a/boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig
+++ b/boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig
@@ -78,5 +78,4 @@ CONFIG_STMP3770_MMU=y
 CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGING=y
 CONFIG_STMP3770_KHICAS=y
 CONFIG_ARM_DCACHE_DISABLE=y
-# CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGING is not set
 # CONFIG_STMP3770_PAGETEST is not set
-- 
2.53.0

